  "stemBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "The point P is (−2, 4) and the vector PQ has components 5 and −3. (a) Determine the coordinates of Q. (b) Write the vector QP as a column vector. (c) Calculate |QP|, giving the answer in exact form."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Think first: Adding a vector to a point moves you along it, so Q is P shifted by the components of PQ."
    },
    {
      "type": "asset",
      "storagePath": "assets/question_visuals/p182_q08.jpg",
      "altText": "Source visual for edmar-csec-p182-q08 from workbook page 182."
    }
  ],
  "solutionSteps": [
    {
      "stepNo": 1,
      "instruction": "Add the vector to the starting point.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Q = (−2 + 5, 4 + (−3))"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: Q = (3, 1)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 2,
      "instruction": "Reverse the vector.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "QP is the same journey travelled backwards, so every component changes sign"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: QP = (−5, 3)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 3,
      "instruction": "Check by subtraction.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "QP = P − Q = (−2 − 3, 4 − 1) = (−5, 3)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: QP confirmed"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 4,
      "instruction": "Apply Pythagoras.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "|QP|² = (−5)² + 3² = 25 + 9"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: |QP|² = 34"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 5,
      "instruction": "Leave the root in exact form.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "34 has no square factors, so the surd does not simplify"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: |QP| = √34"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "strategyBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Add PQ to P's coordinates for Q, reverse the signs for QP, then apply Pythagoras and leave the answer as a surd."
    }
  ],
  "finalAnswerBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "(a) Q = (3, 1)  (b) QP = (−5, 3)  (c) |QP| = √34 (≈ 5.83)"
    }
  ],
  "whyThisWorks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "A vector is a displacement, so applying it to a point relocates that point — the components are simply added to the coordinates. Reversing the direction of travel negates both components, but distance has no direction, so |QP| = |PQ|; both are √34. Squaring removes the negative signs, which is why the reversed vector has exactly the same magnitude."
    }
  ],
